# Immich mutate

## Gate

Load only when the user authorized Immich **and** used an explicit mutate
verb this turn (**delete**, **trash**, **share**, **archive**, **create
album**, **admin**) naming the object(s). Otherwise stay on
`immich-library`. Always pair with `immich-safety` before any mutate call.

No Immich MCP discovered — use Immich REST API or UI only. **Do not invent
MCP tool names.**

## Inventory before mutate

1. Resolve album/asset/person ids from list/search this turn
   (`immich-library`).
2. Prefer trash/archive over permanent delete when silence is enough.
3. State planned action + ids in one line; then call.

## Live API mutate map

| Action | Approach | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Trash / archive assets | asset update / trash endpoints | prefer before hard delete |
| Permanent delete / empty trash | delete endpoints | explicit **delete** + ids |
| Create / update album | albums create/update | named album only |
| Add/remove album assets | album asset endpoints | resolved asset ids |
| Share link create/revoke | shared-link endpoints | public link = exposure risk |
| Admin user / API key | admin endpoints | refuse key dumps; explicit admin verb |

Confirm exact paths against the instance OpenAPI for the resolved Immich
version.

## Defaults

- Prefer trash over permanent delete.
- Prefer private albums over public share links unless the user asked for
  a share link.
- Never bulk-delete across libraries the user did not name.
- State which endpoints/fields you used in the receipt.

## Share-link warning

Public share links expose media to anyone with the URL. Before create:
restate scope (album/assets) and whether the link is public. Prefer
passworded or short-lived links when the API supports them and the user
asked.

## Operator receipt (mutate)

- action (trash/delete/share/album/admin)
- object id(s)
- outcome
- no API keys, passwords, or media bytes

